<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY2-QA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY2-QA-002" ;
  triage:title "D5/AC6 unmet: no test exercises the real transport path (HerdrProcessInvoker/CliIo -> decode_envelope)" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1269-r1 (PR #1269 @ a35154291; Blocking; req-qa ATM-QA-001, independently confirmed). crates/atm-herdr/tests/fake_herdr_modes.rs spawned the fake-Herdr binary directly and asserted only on its stdout; it never routed through HerdrIo/CliIo/HerdrProcessInvoker. decode_envelope (must tolerate unknown JSON fields and CRLF per D5) has exactly one caller, crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_cli.rs:35 (production), and no test invokes it. No test references CliIo or HerdrProcessInvoker. D5 coverage (child-stdout parsing, argv+HERDR_SESSION round-trip through one invoker, binary resolution through the Phase AX path, version replay between calls, unknown-field tolerance, CRLF tolerance) is structurally untested; AC6 unmet. Required correction: integration tests that route through the real production path against the fake-herdr binary (PATH-inject fake-herdr as herdr, or a cfg(test)-only HerdrClientConfig constructor with explicit binary path), covering CRLF, unknown JSON fields, two sessions through one invoker, and version replay across two calls." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-herdr/tests/, crates/atm-herdr/src/transport.rs, crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_cli.rs, docs/plans/phase-ay/sprint-AY.2-*.md D5/AC6" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-06T23:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-06T23:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
